f4 Na5 16. Rac1 bxc3 17. Nxc3 Nc6 18. e5 dxe5 19. Ne4 Bg7 20. Bxc5 h4 21. g4
exf4 22. d4 Qc7 23. Kh1 f5 24. gxf5 gxf5 25. Nc3 f3 26. Rxf3 Bh6 27. Qe1 Bxc1
28. Nd5 Qa5 29. Qxc1 Kf7 30. Ra3 Qb5 31. Rb3 Qe2 32. Nf4 Qf2 33. Nd3 Qe2 34.
Nf4 Qf2 35. Nd3 Qe2 36. Nf4 Qf2 {Source: BCM, July 1936, p314} (36... Qf2 {"By
some inadvertence, in a misconstruction or forgetfulness of Rule 16c. Only
"the Player" has the right to claim. A similar case occurred at Margate at
Easter. White can win by} 37. Bxc6 (37. d5 $1 $18 {Hiarcs} Nd4 38. Re3 $1)
37... Bxc6+ 38. d5 Bxd5+ 39. Nxd5 Qe2 (39... Rbc8 $1 $14 {Hiarcs}) 40. Re3 {.
The exchange was lost in error at move 27, no sacrifice being intended. Morry
deserves credit for giving his doughty opponent so much to think about." (BCM)}
) 1/2-1/2

