{Opening: QP Indian...} 1. d4 {"Winter held a slight advantage throughout, but
cut it too fine. In the end there were R and N each, with Winter a P up. Ns
were exchanged, and then Winter had two passed Ps on his right wing against
Davey's passed a-pawn. A weak advance of the Kt P ruined whatever chance White
had of winning." (BCM) Source: July 1936, p315.} 1/2-1/2

