1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 {... In the latter part of the first week Sir George Thomas
developed an 'equality complex' and drew four games in succession. Several
times he had the advantage in the endgame, but not quite enough, with the
small material left, to force a win against the opponent's careful defence.
This was another case in point. Scource: BCM, July 1936, p318.} 1/2-1/2

