1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 {... Cross held an advantage for a long time,
but it disappeared through a slip after four hours' play. Johnson later became
a piece ahead in a curious situation in which both players had their Rs in
threatening positions. Later Cross won the piece back and was a P ahead, but a
third sitting was saved by the telephone. Source: BCM, July 320.} 1/2-1/2

