1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 {... Winter kept the draw in hand, and the game
quickly boiled down to opposite bishops only as to pieces, with Israel 7 Ps to
6. A draw was reached in 32 moves. Winter had laid himself out a programme by
which he hoped to get 3 points out of his last 4 games, and reached 81/2, a
score which no other player could simultaneously get. Source: BCM, July 1936,
p320.} 1/2-1/2

